.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
A structure representing the standard USB configuration descriptor\&. 

This descriptor is documented in section 9\&.6\&.3 of the USB 3\&.0 specification\&. All multiple-byte fields are represented in host-endian format\&. 
.SH "Field Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "uint8_t libusb_config_descriptor::bDescriptorType"

.PP
Descriptor type\&. Will have value \fBlibusb_descriptor_type::LIBUSB_DT_CONFIG\fP LIBUSB_DT_CONFIG in this context\&. 
.SS "uint8_t libusb_config_descriptor::MaxPower"

.PP
Maximum power consumption of the USB device from this bus in this configuration when the device is fully operation\&. Expressed in units of 2 mA when the device is operating in high-speed mode and in units of 8 mA when the device is operating in super-speed mode\&. 
.SS "const struct \fBlibusb_interface\fP* libusb_config_descriptor::interface"

.PP
Array of interfaces supported by this configuration\&. The length of this array is determined by the bNumInterfaces field\&. 
.SS "const unsigned char* libusb_config_descriptor::extra"

.PP
Extra descriptors\&. If libusb encounters unknown configuration descriptors, it will store them here, should you wish to parse them\&. 
.SS "int libusb_config_descriptor::extra_length"

.PP
Length of the extra descriptors, in bytes\&. Must be non-negative\&. 

